init: bundle templates and improve first-run experience

lf ops init now works. Previously it referenced paths that didn't exist
(a commands/ directory that was never created). Templates are now bundled
under src/loopflow/templates/ and copied to the right places.

The starter set is 6 prompts: design, implement, review, debug, polish,
iterate. Running lf ops init --all includes additional prompts. Templates
are generic—no loopflow-specific references like "use uv run".

Error messages now detect uninitialized repos and suggest lf ops init
instead of showing confusing "create .claude/commands/foo.md" hints.
